// A file that DEFINES main and then CALLS it runs it once, not twice. The entry appends `main()`
// when the file defines one, and a top-level expression statement runs on its own; before the guard
// both fired and every such program printed everything twice. Most `.ssc` files in this repository
// end this way, and not one front fixture did — which is why nothing caught it.
def main(): Unit =
  println("once")

main()
